"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-28T10:33:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-28T11:21:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.7.1\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1060 6GB (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6094) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-9400F CPU @ 2.90GHz (6 threads) - 7.94 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nIn Japanese, the “Fill” mode for `Label` alignment is separated by individual characters.\n\n<img width=\"603\" height=\"498\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4a2b0137-3ee6-4bb5-b80d-befce1798c3b\" />\n\n\nP.S.\nI'm starting to think this isn't a bug. When used for furigana (ruby text), I believe the current behavior is correct.\nIf there's Japanese mixed in, would it look better if the English behaved the same way?\nI might just be misunderstanding this feature to begin with.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSet the `horizontal_alignment` property of the Label node to `Fill`, then paste the following text:\n“日本語 日本語 日本語”\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[label_alignment_fill_japanese_issue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30457860/label_alignment_fill_japanese_issue.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121856/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121856/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"s